---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';

const email = site.contact.email;
const updated = '27 October 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="This site doesn't collect personal data, use cookies or track visitors." bodyClass="is-gallery-page">
  <main id="main" class="page legal">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="tag">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose legal-prose">
      <p>
        This is a personal photography portfolio. It doesn't collect personal data, use cookies, or include analytics,
        tracking or advertising. There are no accounts or forms.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Bryce de Bruyn runs this website. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, run by GitHub, Inc. (United States). Like any web server, GitHub receives
        technical information when you load a page, such as your IP address, browser and the page requested, and may
        keep it in server logs for security and to run the service. I don't have access to these logs. This is needed to
        deliver the site (legal basis: legitimate interest, GDPR art. 6(1)(f)). See
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>No cookies or third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The site sets no cookies. Everything it needs, including fonts, photos and the live ISS orbit data, is served
        from this site itself, so your browser doesn't contact other companies unless you follow an external link (for
        example to YouTube or LinkedIn), where that site's own privacy policy applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Emails you send me</h2>
      <p>
        If you email me, I receive your email address and message in my email account (Gmail, provided by Google) and
        use them only to reply to you. I keep them only as long as needed for our conversation.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR you have the right to access, correct or delete your personal data, and to object to its
        processing. To use these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. If you think your data has been
        handled improperly, you can complain to the Spanish data protection authority, the
        <a href="https://www.aepd.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Agencia Española de Protección de Datos (AEPD)</a>,
        or to the authority in your own country.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this site ever starts collecting anything, this page will be updated first and the date at the top will change.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
